To center a `div` both horizontally and vertically, you can use CSS. Here are a few methods:

### Method 1: Using Flexbox
Flexbox is one of the most straightforward and modern ways to center elements.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Center Div</title>
    <style>
        .container {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh; /* Full viewport height */
        }
        .centered-div {
            width: 200px;
            height: 200px;
            background-color: lightblue;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="centered-div"></div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

